#: GameServer/RpcHandlers.lean:169
msgid "level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: GameServer/RpcHandlers.lean:177
msgid "level completed with warnings… 🎭"
msgstr ""

#: GameServer/RpcHandlers.lean:190
msgid "intermediate goal solved! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:5
msgid "Goals and hypotheses"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `⊢`
#. §1: `h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:7
msgid "A Lean proof is a conversation with a *goal* (after §0) and the *hypotheses* above it.\n"
"Here the hypothesis §1 says exactly what the goal says."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = 3$
#. §1: $x = 3$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:12
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L03_NormNum.lean:13
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:12
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:40
msgid "If §0 then §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact h`
#. §1: `h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:14
msgid "§0 closes the goal when §1 is literally the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:17
msgid "Every proof in this game ends, eventually, with a step like this one."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact h`
#. §1: `h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L01_Exact.lean:19
msgid "§0 closes the goal using a term §1 whose type is exactly the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:5
msgid "Rewriting"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [h]`
#. §1: `h : a = b`
#. §2: `a`
#. §3: `b`
#. §4: `rw [← h]`
#. §5: `b`
#. §6: `a`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:7
msgid "§0 uses an equation §1 to replace §2 by §3 in the goal.\n"
"§4 replaces §5 by §6 instead."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = y$
#. §1: $y = 5$
#. §2: $x = 5$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:12
msgid "If §0 and §1 then §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `«{h₁}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:14
msgid "Rewrite the §0 in the goal using §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h₂}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:16
msgid "The goal is now exactly §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [h]`
#. §1: `h`
#. §2: `rw [h] at h'`
#. §3: `rw [← h]`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L02_Rewrite.lean:19
msgid "§0 rewrites the goal with the equation §1. §2 rewrites a hypothesis\n"
"instead, and §3 rewrites right-to-left."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L03_NormNum.lean:5
msgid "The calculator"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `norm_num`
#. §1: `2 + 2 = 4`
#. §2: `(3 : ℝ) ≠ 5`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L03_NormNum.lean:7
msgid "§0 does arithmetic with explicit numbers: it proves §1 or that\n"
"§2. It is a calculator, not a mathematician. Some worlds switch it off when\n"
"it would do the interesting part of the work for you."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `rw`
#. §2: `norm_num`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L03_NormNum.lean:15
msgid "First get rid of §0 with §1, then let §2 add up."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `norm_num`
#. §1: `2 + 2 = 4`
#. §2: `(1 : ℝ) ≠ 2`
#. §3: `norm_num at h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L03_NormNum.lean:19
msgid "§0 proves goals about explicit numerals (§1, §2). Use\n"
"§3 to simplify a hypothesis."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:5
msgid "And"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h : P ∧ Q`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨hp, hq⟩ := h`
#. §2: `P ∧ Q`
#. §3: `constructor`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:7
msgid "A system of equations is a big \"and\". To *use* §0, split it with\n"
"§1. To *prove* §2, use §3, which leaves two goals."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = 1$
#. §1: $y = 2$
#. §2: $y = 2$
#. §3: $x = 1$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:12
msgid "If §0 and §1, then §2 and §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨hx, hy⟩ := «{h}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:14
msgid "Take §0 apart: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `constructor`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:16
msgid "Now §0 splits the goal into two."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `constructor`
#. §1: `P ∧ Q`
#. §2: `P ↔ Q`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:21
msgid "§0 splits a goal §1 (or §2) into separate goals."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := h`
#. §1: `h : P ∧ Q`
#. §2: `h : ∃ x, P x`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L04_And.lean:23
msgid "§0 takes apart a hypothesis §1 or §2."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:5
msgid "There exists"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∃ x, …`
#. §1: `use 3`
#. §2: `3`
#. §3: `x`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:7
msgid "\"Solve this equation\" is often the goal §0. Prove it by naming a solution:\n"
"§1 puts §2 in place of §3, and you then check that it works."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x$
#. §1: $2x = 6$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:12
msgid "There is a real number §0 with §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `use`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:14
msgid "Which number works? §0 it."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:18
msgid "Many \"find the solution\" questions on the sheets look like this: you supply\n"
"the witness, Lean checks it."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `use a`
#. §1: `∃ x, P x`
#. §2: `a`
#. §3: `P a`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:21
msgid "§0 proves §1 by supplying §2, leaving §3 to prove."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:5
msgid "Not"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `¬ P`
#. §1: `intro hp`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `False`
#. §4: `1 = 2`
#. §5: `False`
#. §6: `norm_num at h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:7
msgid "§0 means \"P leads to a contradiction\". To prove it, §1 assumes §2; your goal\n"
"becomes §3. A hypothesis like §4 gives you §5 via §6."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `≠`
#. §1: `¬ (… = …)`
#. §2: `intro h2`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:14
msgid "§0 is §1. Start with §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `«{h2}»`
#. §2: `rw [«{h}»] at «{h2}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:16
msgid "Substitute what you know about §0 into §1: §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h2}»`
#. §1: `1 = 2`
#. §2: `norm_num at «{h2}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:18
msgid "§0 now claims §1. §2 sees that it is false."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `intro h`
#. §1: `P → Q`
#. §2: `¬ P`
#. §3: `∀ x, …`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:21
msgid "§0 moves an assumption into the context: for goals §1, §2 and §3."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:5
msgid "Or, and case splits"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P ∨ Q`
#. §1: `left`
#. §2: `right`
#. §3: `h : P ∨ Q`
#. §4: `rcases h with hp | hq`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:7
msgid "To prove §0, pick a side with §1 or §2. To use §3, split into\n"
"two cases with §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = 1$
#. §1: $x = 2$
#. §2: $x^2 = 1$
#. §3: $x^2 = 4$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:12
msgid "If §0 or §1, then §2 or §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `rcases «{h}» with h1 | h2`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:14
msgid "Split on §0: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x = 1`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:16
msgid "Here §0. Which side of the goal is true?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `left`
#. §1: `right`
#. §2: `P ∨ Q`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:24
msgid "§0 / §1 choose which side of a goal §2 to prove."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `left`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:26
msgid "See §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rcases h with h1 | h2`
#. §1: `h : P ∨ Q`
#. §2: `rcases h with ⟨a, b⟩`
#. §3: `∧`
#. §4: `∃`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:28
msgid "§0 splits §1 into two cases; §2\n"
"takes apart §3 and §4."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:5
msgid "Vectors and matrices"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $\\mathbb R^n$
#. §1: `![a, b, …]`
#. §2: `!![a, b; c, d]`
#. §3: `;`
#. §4: `A *ᵥ v`
#. §5: `ext i`
#. §6: `fin_cases i`
#. §7: `0`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:7
msgid "In this game a vector in §0 is written §1 and a matrix\n"
"§2 (rows separated by §3). §4 is the matrix–vector product.\n"
"\n"
"Two vectors are equal when they agree in every component. §5 asks you to prove that,\n"
"and §6 splits into one goal per component (numbered from §7)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\7\\end{pmatrix}$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:16
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:34
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:43
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:14
msgid "§0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ext i`
#. §1: `fin_cases i`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:18
msgid "Compare component by component: §0, then §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `norm_num [mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:21
msgid "Row 1 times the vector. §0 unfolds\n"
"the product and adds it up."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ext i`
#. §1: `ext i j`
#. §2: `i`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:26
msgid "§0 reduces an equation between vectors (or matrices, §1) to one component §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `fin_cases i`
#. §1: `i : Fin n`
#. §2: `0, …, n-1`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:28
msgid "§0 splits a goal about §1 into one goal per value §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A *ᵥ v`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:30
msgid "§0: the matrix–vector product."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `u ⬝ᵥ v`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Vectors.lean:32
msgid "§0: the dot product."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:5
msgid "Commit, then prove"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `¬ P ∨ P`
#. §1: `left`
#. §2: `right`
#. §3: $x$
#. §4: $x \\cdot x = x$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:8
msgid "Many sheet questions say *\"true or false?\"*. In this game they look like this: the goal\n"
"is §0. You commit with §1 (false) or §2 (true), then prove your choice.\n"
"Choose wrong and you will get stuck — which is the lesson.\n"
"\n"
"**Claim:** for every real §3, §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x$
#. §1: $x \\cdot x = x$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:16
msgid "True or false: for every real §0, §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = 2$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:18
msgid "Decide first. Is it true for §0?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `intro h`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:20
msgid "To refute a \"for all\", assume it with §0 and find a counterexample."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `have h2 := «{h}» 2`
#. §1: $x = 2$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:22
msgid "§0 specialises it to §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `have h : P := proof`
#. §1: `have h := f a`
#. §2: `f`
#. §3: `a`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_Decide.lean:26
msgid "§0 adds a new fact; §1 specialises §2 to §3."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics.lean:12
msgid "Lean Basics"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics.lean:14
msgid "Before any linear algebra: the handful of Lean moves every later proof uses. Nine short\n"
"levels, about twenty minutes."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:5
msgid "Zero times anything"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $V$
#. §1: $+$
#. §2: $\\cdot$
#. §3: $0 \\cdot \\vec v = \\vec 0$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:7
msgid "A vector space is a set §0 with §1 and §2 satisfying Hefferon's ten conditions\n"
"(Definition Two.I.1.1). Your inventory holds just the conditions this proof needs, plus one cancellation law. There is no automation.\n"
"\n"
"Our first theorem is Lemma Two.I.1.16 (1): §3.\n"
"It is *not* one of the axioms; we must earn it."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $\\vec v$
#. §1: $0 \\cdot \\vec v = \\vec 0$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:17
msgid "For every vector §0, §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $0 = 0 + 0$
#. §1: $0 \\cdot v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:20
msgid "Idea: §0. What does that say about §1?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $0 \\cdot v + 0 \\cdot v = 0 \\cdot v + \\vec 0$
#. §1: `have`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:21
msgid "So §0. State that with §1, then cancel."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `have h : (0:ℝ) • «{v}» + (0:ℝ) • «{v}» = (0:ℝ) • «{v}» + 0`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:22
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:22
msgid "§0"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `← add_smul`
#. §1: `add_zero`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:24
msgid "Rewrite the left side with §0, then §1 twice."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $0 \\cdot v$
#. §1: `«{h}»`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:26
msgid "Cancel §0 on the left of both sides of §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `zero_smul_eq_zero`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:31
msgid "That is exactly the textbook proof, line for line. From now on §0 is in\n"
"your inventory."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $(r+s)\\cdot v = r\\cdot v + s\\cdot v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:36
msgid "§0 — Hefferon's condition (7)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $v + \\vec 0 = v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:38
msgid "§0 — Hefferon's condition (4)."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L01_ZeroSmul.lean:44
msgid "Mathlib's version; disabled here."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:5
msgid "Inverses are unique"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $w$
#. §1: $w'$
#. §2: $v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:14
msgid "**Problem Sheet 4, Question 3.** In a vector space every element has an additive\n"
"inverse. Can some elements have two or more?\n"
"\n"
"Decide what you believe, then prove it. Suppose §0 and §1 are both inverses of §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $w$
#. §1: $w'$
#. §2: $v$
#. §3: $w = w'$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:23
msgid "If §0 and §1 are both additive inverses of §2, then §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $w = w + 0 = w + (v + w') = (w + v) + w' = 0 + w' = w'$
#. §1: `calc`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:26
msgid "Write §0.\n"
"A §1 block lets you write exactly that chain."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $w$
#. §1: $w'$
#. §2: $v$
#. §3: $w = w + (v + w') = (w + v) + w' = w'$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:36
msgid "**Answer to Sheet 4 Q3: no.** If §0 and §1 are both inverses of §2 then\n"
"§3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $(a + b) + c = a + (b + c)$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:41
msgid "§0 — Hefferon's condition (3)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `calc`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:45
msgid "§0 writes a chain of equalities, each with its own justification."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:50
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L02_NegUnique.lean:52
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:38
msgid "disabled"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:5
msgid "Minus one times a vector"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $(-1)\\cdot\\vec v + \\vec v = \\vec 0$
#. §1: $(-1)\\cdot\\vec v$
#. §2: $\\vec v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:7
msgid "Lemma Two.I.1.16 (2): §0, i.e. §1 *is* the\n"
"additive inverse of §2. Your two earlier theorems are now tools."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $v$
#. §1: $1 \\cdot v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:17
msgid "Idea: write the second §0 as §1, then combine the scalars."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `nth_rw 2 [← one_smul ℝ «{v}»]`
#. §1: `rw [← add_smul]`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:18
msgid "§0, then §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `-v`
#. §1: `(-1)•v`
#. §2: `simp`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:27
msgid "Now §0 and §1 are interchangeable — the game will let §2 do this from here on."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $1 \\cdot v = v$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:29
msgid "§0 — Hefferon's condition (10)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `nth_rw n [h]`
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:31
msgid "§0 rewrites only the n-th occurrence."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $-a + a = 0$
#: Game/Levels/Axioms/L03_NegOneSmul.lean:33
msgid "§0 (in ℝ, or in any group)."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms.lean:6
msgid "The Ten Conditions"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Axioms.lean:8
msgid "Every theorem in this game will ultimately rest on the ten conditions of\n"
"Definition Two.I.1.1. In this world you derive the first consequences by hand."
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:5
msgid "Echelon"
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:6
msgid "**Echelon** is Oxford's first-year Linear Algebra course (MT2026, after Hefferon) as a game.\n"
"Every problem-sheet question is a level. Solve them in Lean, then export your own proofs\n"
"for your tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:13
msgid "Based on Jim Hefferon's *Linear Algebra* (4th ed.) and the MT2026 problem sheets.\n"
"Built on lean4game and Mathlib."
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:20
msgid "Hefferon in Lean"
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:21
msgid "The Oxford first-year Linear Algebra course, as a game: every problem-sheet question is a level."
msgstr ""
